3 x d x & =8 v d v
\end{aligned}
\end{aligned}$<br/>Integrating both sides
$\begin{aligned}
3\left[\frac{x^2}{2}\right]_2^{10} & =8\left[\frac{v^2}{2}\right]_0^v \\
\frac{3}{2}\left[10^2-2^2\right] & =4 v^2 \\
\frac{3}{2} \times 96 & =4 v^2 \\
v & =6 \mathrm{~m} / \mathrm{s}
\end{aligned}$

Time taken by the small ball to return to the hands of the juggler is $\frac{2 \mathrm{~V}}{g}=\frac{2 \times 20}{10}=4 \mathrm{~s}$. So, he is throwing the balls after 1 s each. Let at some instant, he throws the ball number 4 . Before 1 s of throwing it, he throws ball 3 . So, the height of ball 3 is
$\begin{aligned}
h & =u t-\frac{1}{2} g t^2 \\
h_3 & =20 \times 1-\frac{1}{2}
\end{aligned}$<br/>Before 2 s , he throws ball 2 . So, the height of ball 2 is
$h_2=20 \times 2-\frac{1}{2} \times 10(2)^2=20 \mathrm{~m}$<br/>Before 3 s , he throws ball 1 . So, the height of ball 1 is
$\begin{aligned}
& h_1=20 \times 3-\frac{1}{2} \times 10(3)^2 \\
\Rightarrow \quad & h_1=15 \mathrm{~m}
\end{aligned}$
